The Regulations on Establishment and Operation of Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy are hereby repealed.
Article 3 (Special cases concerning dedicated institutions)
"Requirements prescribed by Presidential Decree, including organization and personnel" in Article 3 of the Addenda to the Framework Act on the Development of Artificial Intelligence and the Creation of a foundation for Trust (Act No. 20676) refers to the requirements prescribed in each subparagraphs of Article 18(1).
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning transfer of functions of the Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy)
(1) The Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy established under Article 2 of the former Regulations on Establishment and Operation of Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy (hereinafter referred to as "the former Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy”) at the time this Decree enters into force shall be deemed the Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy established under Article 7 of the Act.
(2) The functions of the former Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy at the time this Decree enters into force shall be assumed by the Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy established under Article 7 of the Act.
(3) Any deliberation, resolution, or other act that was conducted by the former Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy, or any act that was directed toward the former Council before this Decree enters into force in accordance with the former Regulations on Establishment and Operation of Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy, shall be deemed to be a deliberation, resolution, or other act conducted by, or an act directed toward, the Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy established under Article 7 of the Act. 
(4) Members commissioned under Article 3(3)4 of the former Regulations on Establishment and Operation of Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy before this Decree enters into force shall be deemed to have been commissioned under Article 7(4)4 of the Act, and the term of office of the commissioned members shall be the remaining period of their term.
Article 5 (Transitional measures concerning secretariat of Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy)
(1) The secretariat of the Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy established under Article 10 of the former Regulations on Establishment and Operation of Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy at the time this Decree enters into force shall be deemed the secretariat of the Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy under Article 6 of the Act.
(2) The functions and budget of the secretariat of the Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy established under Article 10 of the former Regulations on Establishment and Operation of Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy, at the time this Decree enters into force, shall be assumed by the secretariat of the Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy under Article 6.
Article 6 (Transitional measures concerning seconded public officials)
A public official, executive officer, or employee who has been seconded to or is concurrently serving in the secretariat of the Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy in accordance with Article 11 of the former Regulations on Establishment and Operation of Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy, at the time this Decree enters into force, shall be deemed to be a public official, executive officer, or employee who has been seconded to or is concurrently serving in the secretariat of the Presidential Council on National Artificial Intelligence Strategy in accordance with Article 6(3).
